					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-586169#post-2010295</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-586169/olympia#post-2010295</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Apr 2014 20:04:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Aelanna</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>334454</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The original Olympia tales, which were written in the oldest days of the modern SCP Wiki, represented a type of fiction that never really took off and is completely out of vogue these days. Mad-scientist type tales involving mixing skips just don't work, they break the tone of the site, and Olympia itself has more or less been swept under a rug and forgotten about. This was Roget's attempt to tie off that series and give it some semblance of closure.</p> <p>To reiterate: most peoples' canons don't include Olympia. She was a bit of a Mary Sue and honestly just didn't work out.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
